=== Minion Skins & Minion Chair ===
{{Main|Minion Skins|Minion Chair}}
'''Minion Skins''' override a specific minion's appearance, but do not affect performance. The '''Minion Chair''' is a [[Furniture]] item that minions can sit on. Sitting minions do not work or take up [[Minions#Minion Slots|Minion Slots]]. A minion skin cannot be applied to a sitting minion.

== Mechanics ==
=== Time Between Actions ===
Minions with a description that includes '''Time Between Actions''' will generate collectable items every other action. For example, if a Tier I {{Item|Cobblestone Minion}} has a Time Between Actions of {{Green|14}} seconds, it will generate {{Item|Cobblestone|1}} every {{Green|28}} seconds, not {{Green|14}} seconds.

==== Time Between Actions Calculation ====
Minion speed boosts are additive. The minion's '''Time Between Actions''' are decreased according to the following formula:

<math>\text{Time Between Actions}=\frac{\text{Base Time Between Actions}}{1 + \text{Combined Speed Boost Percentage}}</math>

For a Tier XI {{Item|Clay Minion}} with {{Item|Enchanted Coal}}, the Base Time Between Actions is {{Green|16}} seconds, and the speed increase from the {{Item|Enchanted Coal}} is {{Green|+10%}}, so the new Time Between Actions would be as follows:

<math>\text{Time Between Actions}=\frac{16\,\text{seconds}}{100\%+10\%}\approx 14.55\,\text{seconds}</math>

=== Mob Spawning ===
[[File:2019-12-15 20.47.57.png|thumb|220x220px|A two-dimensional representation of where a mob can spawn around a minion (top block height is based on the height of mob).]]

The mechanics of '''[[Mobs|Mob]] Spawning''' minions are similar to that of [[mcw:Monster Spawner|Monster Spawners]] in vanilla ''Minecraft'':

* The "Ideal Layout" shows the general spawning area for mobs around a minion.
* Minions can spawn mobs only within a {{Green|5x5}} area centered around them, unless they have a {{Item|Minion Expander}}.
* The vertical range in which they spawn is {{Green|6}} blocks ({{Green|3}} below, {{Green|2}} above, and {{Green|1}} at eye level with the minion).
* As long as there is a block for them to spawn on and spawning will not cause them to take suffocation damage, they will spawn in accordance with the minion's normal spawning times.
* Mobs that are wider than {{Green|1}} block ({{MobSprite|Slime}}s, {{MobSprite|Magma Cube}}s, {{MobSprite|Ghast}}s, etc.) are limited by the horizontal range, but they will still spawn partially inside nearby walls and may possibly escape.
* If a mob is outside of a minion's range, it will not kill it automatically and collect the loot.

